er mark at the start is accepted. Network and protocol faults (a bad address, a cut-off answer, a reset) print only the name of the error type, never the address or a header. The address is also refused when it holds a user name part (`@`) or a space, tab or line break, and unless the text between `//` and the first `/` is exactly a host name (letters, digits, dots, hyphens) or a bracketed IPv6 address, optionally followed by one `:port` with a port from 1 to 65535 (so a backslash, a second port, text after a bracket, an empty port and `:0` are refused, and a non-ASCII host name must be given in its ASCII form). n8n's own names such as `N8N_PORT` are n8n's, not this repository's; they appear in `docs/n8n-recipe.md`. `scripts/run_live_check.py` takes command-line flags, not settings names: `--key-file`, `--base-url`, `--ledger`, `--cap-run`, `--cap-total`, `--price-date` and one `--model ID=IN_PRICE,OUT_PRICE` per model, and optionally `--max-tokens`, `--effort`, `--timeout` (see the text at the top of the file).
